7d24h-templates - licensing overview

This repository is not under one single license. Every template directory
carries its own license file, and that file is what applies to the files
of that template. The full texts of the licenses used below are in
LICENSES/.

  Path                               License
  ---------------------------------  ---------------------------------------
  typage/<id>/, spage/<id>/,         The template's own license file
  mpage/<id>/                        (LICENSE in the template directory,
                                     named by "license.file" in its
                                     manifest.json). It lists every file of
                                     the template with its license.

  tools/, schemas/, .github/         BSD-2-Clause
                                     (LICENSES/BSD-2-Clause.txt)

  Everything else written by 7D24H   CC0-1.0
  (README.md, AUTHORING.md,          (LICENSES/CC0-1.0.txt)
  categories.json, catalog/, this
  file)

Templates written by 7D24H (their samples, bibliographies, manifest.json and
typage.json) are released under CC0-1.0, so papers and documents written
from them carry no obligation towards 7D24H.

Third-party files inside a template - for example a conference's or
publisher's official document class or bibliography style - keep their
original license and copyright notices and are redistributed unmodified.
7D24H does not relicense them. Their licenses are named in the template's
own license file. Placing templates under different licenses side by side
in this repository, or in one download, does not put any file under
another file's license.

Licenses that are fine for system templates without further review:
CC0-1.0, CC-BY-4.0, MIT, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, Apache-2.0, LPPL-1.2,
LPPL-1.3a, LPPL-1.3c, OFL-1.1. Copyleft (GPL, LGPL, AGPL, CC BY-SA),
non-commercial (CC BY-NC), no-derivatives (CC BY-ND) and files without a
license are flagged by tools/validate.mjs for review before release; such
venues are offered as "official, obtain it yourself" instead.

Template license files are maintained by the template operators and may be
completed at any time; a license-only change is re-published under the
same template version.

Copyright (c) 2026, 7D24H group, for the parts written by 7D24H.
